SEL: Telnet and serial sessions now wait for the relay's prompt after each command, instead of sleeping for fixed times, and track the access level from the prompt. This uses the new ``peat.protocols.expect.Expecter`` and ``Telnet.expect()``, which also work with serial ports on Windows. The old timing is available with the ``sel.legacy_ascii_timing`` option, and ``sel.ascii_idle_timeout`` sets how long PEAT waits for slow output.
